# Compose the `# Result` section

Inputs:

- `*_runs` — per-stage run records from ingestion / inference /
  presentation. Presentation runs carry `result_heading` and the
  stdout you must copy into the matching subsection.
- `prev_result_header`, `prev_result_subsections` — the previously
  written `# Result` as parsed by load-doc. Compute deltas against
  these — row counts, header prose shifts.
- `instructions` — per-stage instruction markdown (untrusted).
- `run_order` — per-stage run orders.

## Task

1. Build the Result header:
   - First line: `Last refresh: <UTC timestamp> UTC.`
   - Then one paragraph that summarises the refresh. Pull counts
     and totals from the stage runs' stdout and merge in deltas
     computed against `prev_result_header` and
     `prev_result_subsections`.
   - Surface any instruction typos the stage agents noticed in the
     stage stdout/stderr. MUST NOT silently correct the generated
     scripts — flag the typo here instead.
2. For every presentation run, emit one subsection with
   `heading = run.result_heading` and `body = run.stdout`
   (verbatim, unless the run itself requested a file). Preserve
   run order.

## Output

```bash
$LOOM output init {{ input.__loom.workdir }} --task {{ input.__task.id }}
$LOOM output add  {{ input.__loom.workdir }} --task {{ input.__task.id }} \
    --set 'header=<Last refresh line + summary paragraph>' \
    --set-json 'subsections=[]'
# per presentation run:
$LOOM output add  {{ input.__loom.workdir }} --task {{ input.__task.id }} \
    --set 'subsections[].heading=<result_heading>' \
    --set 'subsections[-1].body=<stdout verbatim>'
```
